    "title": "Gates mark the end and beginning of an era - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kristie Bowles kbowles@tiogapublishing.com ,\n12 hours ago MANSFIELD – Five years ago the Gate House in Mansfield sat dark and abandoned by Smythe Park, “Cold and lonely” as Steve McCloskey put it. At that time, the gate house had no electricity and was slated for demolition by the Southern Tioga School District, which owns it, because it was a safety liability and had no usable purpose. Some residents noticed the forlorn state of the building and approached the STSD for permission to just put a light inside. Read full article",
